el disease, further emphasizing their expertise and influence in the field of nutrition.", "MALDHI H:Author of the article on dysphagia warning signs and management published in Br J Nurs in 2016", "JANSSON-KNODELL CI:Co-author of the review on making dysphagia easier to swallow published in Mayo Clin Proc in 2017", "CODIPILLY CH:Co-author of the review on making dysphagia easier to swallow published in Mayo Clin Proc in 2017", "LEGGETT CL:Co-author of the review on making dysphagia easier to swallow published in Mayo Clin Proc in 2017", "VELASCO MM:", "ROSA ANA ASHBAUGH ENGUÍDANOS:Rosa Ana Ashbaugh Enguídanos is a professional dedicated to the study and promotion of oral hygiene and its significance in health care. In addition to her work in oral hygiene, she is also a researcher focused on oropharyngeal dysphagia, specifically exploring its screening methods. Through her dual involvement in these areas, she contributes to enhancing understanding and practices related to oral health and swallowing disorders.", "ESPEN GUIDELINES 2017:The ESPEN Guidelines 2017 provide recommendations for the management and treatment of dysphagia.", "BARNES-JEWISH HOSPITAL STROKE DYSPHAGIA SCREEN:The Barnes-Jewish Hospital Stroke Dysphagia Screen is a specific method for assessing dysphagia in stroke patients.", "SWALLOW QUESTIONNAIRE:The Swallow Questionnaire is a tool utilized to assess swallowing difficulties in patients. It is specifically designed to measure the quality of life and subjective symptoms experienced by individuals with dysphagia, providing valuable insights into their condition and helping to guide treatment decisions.", "EATING ASSESSMENT TOOL-10:The Eating Assessment Tool-10 is a screening tool specifically designed to assess dysphagia in patients. It functions as a self-evaluation scale that enables individuals to evaluate their own clinical symptoms related to dysphagia. This tool is instrumental in identifying difficulties in swallowing, thereby facilitating appropriate clinical interventions.", "PREDYCES STUDY:The PREDyCES Study is a comprehensive research initiative that investigates the prevalence and costs associated with malnutrition in hospitalized patients, specifically focusing on those with diabetes mellitus and dysphagia. This study aims to analyze the extent of hospital malnutrition among these patient groups, highlighting the significant health and economic implications of this condition in a hospital setting. Through its multifaceted approach, the PREDyCES Study seeks to provide valuable insights into the challenges posed by malnutrition in healthcare, ultimately contributing to improved patient care and resource allocation.", "DYSFAGIA:Dysfagia, also known as dysphagia, is a medical condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing. This condition can significantly impact patients' health and quality of life, leading to serious complications such as aspiration, malnutrition, and dehydration, particularly in patients with conditions like ELA (Early Life Autism) and those who have suffered strokes. Various organizations provide resources related to dysphagia, and it can be assessed using a range of screening methods, scales, and tools designed to improve nutritional recommendations and enhance patient independence. Additionally, technological interventions, including virtual reality, have been explored as potential solutions to address the challenges associated with dysphagia."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}